Negative control for the `Filter` renderer's DISPATCH.

Points the Verified element at the generic `Control` type, so the filter bar
draws JSONForms' default control instead of the dispatching Filter renderer.
Any assertion that reads the tri-state's own positions goes red; one that only
asserts the form rendered stays green.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

diff --git a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
--- a/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
+++ b/packages/headless/src/modules/client-email/client-email.schemas.ts
@@ -251,7 +251,7 @@
         options: { width: "full" }
       },
       {
-        type: "Filter",
+        type: "Control",
         scope: "#/properties/filters/properties/verified",
         i18n: "form.verified_filter",
         options: { treatment: "button-group" }
